+<h2>84. AppError subclasses in packages/shared keep their own prototype, so <code>instanceof</code> on them is no longer always false (KS-1467)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> KS-1467, the packages/shared half (the services/auth half is a separate change): the constructor of <code>AppError</code> in <code>packages/shared/src/errors/index.ts</code> ended with <code>Object.setPrototypeOf(this, AppError.prototype)</code>, which reset every subclass instance to the base prototype. So <code>err instanceof NotFoundError</code>, and the same test on the other eight subclasses and on <code>DocumentNotFoundError</code>, was always false. The line now reads <code>Object.setPrototypeOf(this, new.target.prototype)</code>. A local model (the Spark, DeepSeek V4 Flash) wrote the patch; its checker passed 7 of 7 and the patch is byte-identical to the drafter&rsquo;s golden. It was applied here strictly and unchanged. </td></tr><tr><td>One product line changes (+1 / &minus;1). The new test is <code>packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks1467-shared-app-error-subclasses-keep-their-own-prototype.test.ts</code> (vitest, 29 cells). A search of non-test source in <code>services/</code> and <code>packages/</code> finds one code use of <code>instanceof</code> on one of these subclass names, in <code>services/auth/src/middleware/errorHandler.ts</code>, which defines its own classes and does not import these (plus one comment in <code>passwordLoginGate.ts</code>). No tier timing or budget in these documents moves.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>84.1 Red-first, and the figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="4"><strong>Measured at base <code>bd6697e079fc</code>, 2026-10-28 (UTC), Kamil&rsquo;s MacBook Pro (Mac14,5, Apple M2 Max, 32 GB), shared with other sessions.</strong></td><td> vitest 4.1.12, TypeScript 5.9.3, npm 11.19.0, each read from the installed package. Host Node <strong>v26.8.1</strong>, which is <strong>not</strong> an LTS line, and no Node 24 run was made, so every figure below is a Node 26 measurement. </td></tr>
+<tr><td>The new file against the unfixed <code>errors/index.ts</code>: <strong>19 failed / 10 passed</strong> of 29. Every red is an <code>AssertionError</code> (P1 and P2 for nine classes each, and P3, the <code>DocumentNotFoundError</code> chain); the ten control cells C1 and C2 pass at base, as designed. With the fix: <strong>29 / 29</strong>.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>packages/shared suite by cell name: <strong>54 files / 1034 cells, 1 failed</strong> at the base; <strong>55 files / 1063 cells, 1 failed</strong> with the change. 0 cells vanished, 29 are new, 0 changed status. The one failure is the same cell on both sides: <code>wallet-signature.test.ts</code> &ldquo;accepts a valid wallet signature over the message&rdquo;. It fails on Node 26 because <code>cbor.encode</code> truncates every output to one byte there (measured: <code>encode([1,2,3])</code> returns <code>83</code>, not <code>83010203</code>); KS 1727 and KS 1739 track it.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Type-check: <code>tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json</code> rc 0. A child tsconfig with <code>exclude</code> emptied compiled 1575 files, 57 of them under <code>__tests__</code>, the new test among them; it reports 24 errors in other test files (top-level await and <code>import.meta</code> under the package&rsquo;s commonjs module setting) and none in the two files of this change; a planted type error in the same program is reported (rc 2). Lint: <code>eslint</code> on the two files rc 0; <code>npm run lint</code> for the package exits 1 on a pre-existing <code>no-control-regex</code> error in <code>middleware/index.ts</code> (36 problems, none in these files; recorded in <code>BACKLOG.md</code>).</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h3>84.2 What the cells prove, and what they do not</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>The class hierarchy, not any service.</strong></td><td> The cells prove the prototype of an instance of each of the nine subclasses and of <code>DocumentNotFoundError</code> (a two-level subclass), that every instance is still an <code>AppError</code> and an <code>Error</code> with its status, and that <code>errorHandler</code> still answers a <code>ValidationError</code> with its details and a 422. The test imports the package by its source path; it runs no service. </td></tr><tr><td>Not measured: the suites of the other services that import these classes from <code>@secuura/shared</code> (only the packages/shared suite was run), the services/auth half of KS-1467, a running stack, the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a Node 24 LTS run, and any deploy. None of them is claimed as passing.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>84.3 Running it</h3>
+<pre><code>cd Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared &amp;&amp; npx vitest run src/__tests__/ks1467-shared-app-error-subclasses-keep-their-own-prototype.test.ts   # 29 cells, rc 0
+cd Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared &amp;&amp; npx vitest run                                                                                    # 55 files / 1063 cells; 1 failed on Node 26 (wallet-signature, KS 1727)
+cd Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared &amp;&amp; npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json                                                                 # rc 0</code></pre>
